      * Complementary suite on LEGACY: covers what TSTLEG does not
      * touch (the WRITE in the EVALUATE, CALL without a mock, content
      * of the REWRITE, boundary keys, leftover WS-B on INVALID KEY,
      * the EXIT-PARA paragraph and initial values).
       TESTSUITE LEGACYAI 'Legacy: additional branches and limits'
       PROGRAM LEGACY

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01  T-REC.
           05  T-KEY              PIC X(4).
           05  T-DATA             PIC X(20).

       BEFORE-EACH
           MOVE ZERO TO WS-B
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-GRP WS-TIME WS-FS T-REC
           MOVE "N" TO END-OF-FILE
       END-BEFORE

       TESTCASE 'invalid key: no copy, WS-B 4 and clock'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   MOVE "K009" TO M-KEY
                   MOVE "MUST NOT BE COPIED" TO M-DATA
                   SET CBLT-AT-END TO TRUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               CONTINUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '23595999'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'Y'
           EXPECT WS-GRP TO BE SPACES
      * WS-B is still 0: ELSE MOVE 4 and the PERFORM VARYING exits at 4
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 4
           EXPECT WS-TIME TO BE '23595999'
           VERIFY CLOCK HAPPENED 3 TIMES
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY WRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY REWRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY START MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY DELETE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY CLOSE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE

      * The body of the NOT ON EXCEPTION (ADD 1) runs after the mock of
      * the CALL; WS-B is left at 0 so that it ends up at 1 (WHEN 1).
       TESTCASE 'WHEN 1 branch: WRITE from WS-GRP'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   MOVE "XXXX" TO M-KEY
                   MOVE "SYNTHETIC ADD 01" TO M-DATA
               ON WRITE
                   MOVE M-REC TO T-REC
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               MOVE 0 TO WS-B
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '00000000'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 1
           EXPECT T-KEY TO BE 'XXXX'
           EXPECT T-DATA TO BE 'SYNTHETIC ADD 01'
           EXPECT WS-FS TO BE '00'
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY WRITE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY REWRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY CLOCK NEVER HAPPENED

      * REVIEWED: the CALL to NOSUCH does fail and shows "not found",
      * but GnuCOBOL binds the NOT ON EXCEPTION to the preceding DISPLAY
      * (which does not fail) and not to the CALL, so the ADD 1 runs
      * anyway: WS-B ends at 2 and the REWRITE is executed. Actual
      * behavior of the program under this compiler, not of Cobalto.
       TESTCASE 'unmocked CALL to NOSUCH: NOT ON EXCEPTION'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   MOVE "XXXX" TO M-KEY
                   MOVE "NO PROGRAM 03" TO M-DATA
               ON REWRITE
                   MOVE M-REC TO T-REC
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '00000000'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT WS-PROG TO BE 'NOSUCH'
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 2
           EXPECT T-KEY TO BE 'XXXX'
           EXPECT T-DATA TO BE 'NO PROGRAM 03'
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY WRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY REWRITE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE

       TESTCASE 'REWRITE branch writes the record that was read'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   MOVE "XXXX" TO M-KEY
                   MOVE "SYNTHETIC CHANGE 02" TO M-DATA
               ON REWRITE
                   MOVE M-REC TO T-REC
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               CONTINUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '00000000'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 2
           EXPECT T-KEY TO BE 'XXXX'
           EXPECT T-DATA TO BE 'SYNTHETIC CHANGE 02'
           EXPECT WS-FS TO BE '00'
           VERIFY REWRITE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY CLOCK NEVER HAPPENED

       TESTCASE 'lowercase key xxxx does not trigger the CALL'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   MOVE "xxxx" TO M-KEY
                   MOVE SPACES TO M-DATA
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               CONTINUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '11111111'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT WS-KEY TO BE 'xxxx'
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 4
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY CLOCK HAPPENED 3 TIMES
           VERIFY WRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY REWRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED

       TESTCASE 'blank record: valid read, ELSE IF branch'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   MOVE SPACES TO M-REC
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               CONTINUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '22222222'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'N'
           EXPECT WS-KEY TO BE SPACES
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 4
           EXPECT WS-TIME TO BE '22222222'
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY CLOCK HAPPENED 3 TIMES

       TESTCASE 'READ INTO copies all of M-DATA to WS-DATA'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   MOVE "K777" TO M-KEY
                   MOVE "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRST" TO M-DATA
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               CONTINUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '00000000'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT WS-KEY TO BE 'K777'
           EXPECT WS-DATA TO BE 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRST'
           EXPECT WS-DATA TO CONTAIN 'QRST'
           EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'N'

      * REVIEW: WS-B is not initialized in MAIN; on INVALID KEY it
      * keeps its previous value. With 1 the CALL path is taken.
       TESTCASE 'INVALID KEY with leftover WS-B 1: does the CALL'
           MOVE 1 TO WS-B
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   SET CBLT-AT-END TO TRUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               CONTINUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '00000000'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'Y'
           EXPECT WS-GRP TO BE SPACES
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 2
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY REWRITE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY WRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY CLOCK NEVER HAPPENED

      * REVIEW: leftover WS-B 2 with INVALID KEY goes into the ELSE IF
      * (MOVE 3) and the PERFORM VARYING leaves it at 4.
       TESTCASE 'INVALID KEY with leftover WS-B 2: MOVE 3'
           MOVE 2 TO WS-B
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   SET CBLT-AT-END TO TRUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               CONTINUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '12000000'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'Y'
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 4
           EXPECT WS-TIME TO BE '12000000'
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY CLOCK HAPPENED 3 TIMES
           VERIFY WRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY REWRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED

       TESTCASE 'START without INVALID KEY: no jump to EXIT-PARA'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   MOVE "K002" TO M-KEY
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               CONTINUE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '00000000'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           VERIFY PARAGRAPH MAIN HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY PARAGRAPH EXIT-PARA NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY START MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY DELETE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE

       TESTCASE 'EXIT-PARA paragraph only executes EXIT'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM EXIT-PARA
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE ZEROS
           EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'N'
           EXPECT WS-GRP TO BE SPACES
           VERIFY PARAGRAPH EXIT-PARA HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY OPEN MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY CLOSE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED

       TESTCASE 'initial values of WS-PROG and WS-MSG'
           EXPECT WS-PROG TO BE 'NOSUCH'
           EXPECT WS-MSG TO CONTAIN 'hello, world.'
           EXPECT WS-MSG TO CONTAIN 'final period'
